    "narrative": "For LawDog on this July 3rd slate, our offensive core is headlined by **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) and **Luis Arraez** (69.53), who both benefit immensely from a favorable matchup against Feltner. **Lawrence Butler** is our strongest play, leveraging a high-ceiling 3-hole spot against a 4.70 xERA starter, while **Luis Arraez** provides high-floor production at the top of the order, bolstered by excellent park factors. **Jung Hoo Lee** (68.02) rounds out our elite tier, as the 5-hole hitter capitalizes on the same vulnerable pitching matchup. Meanwhile, **Jonathan Aranda** (66.98) earns a strong recommendation due to a prime batting order placement and a solid 0.378 xwOBA, proving that even with a neutral park, his skill-based projections provide significant utility in our 5x5 build.\n\nOur most difficult decision centered on **Gavin Sheets**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 45.35 efficiency score. While he holds a platoon edge against Ohtani, the raw projection was stifled by the pitcher's elite skill profile (3.37 xERA) and the uncertainty surrounding his confirmed batting order. Consequently, we opted to bench him in favor of the higher-scoring profiles provided by **Dylan Beavers** (62.87) and **Daulton Varsho** (58.76). We must monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh** (42.78), who faces the toughest matchup of the day against Cease; while his score is sufficient to warrant a start, his low floor demands caution given the high-end talent opposing him. We continue to manage our bench depth as **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** remain sidelined, forcing us to rely on our active roster to maintain our competitive edge in the scarcity categories.",
